Hello everybody!  Since this is my first post here, a short
introduction:  I've played Nethack inconsequently for fun many years
now; half a year ago, I finally managed to ascend Lator, a chaotic male
human wizard (details on request).  In one earlier game, I've arrived
blindfolded at the castle, was so frightened by the rows of monsters I
detected by ESP that I saved, and eventually lost that game due to
switching computers…  So I survived 100% of the games in which I got to
the castle.  ;-)

Pe dată de 2010-12-03 12:14, Borek Lupoměský a scris:
> Ascension of a Monk
> [...]
Congratulations!  Monks do have some drawbacks.  I'd probably not have
hidden that AoLS inside the bag, though…

> Next role will be lawful human male Priest.
I'm playing priests a lot.  Gratis BCU detection is the detail I like
most about them.  Gives you more than just easy armour bonuses in the
early game.  And with all the holy water, learning spells becomes so simple!

Right now I have a very promising chaotic elven priestess named Seriva.
 She's quite a lucky girl, already with AC-9 (no DSM or divine
protection involved yet).  And that on DL6 of the main dungeon, having
made only a brief detour into the top mine level.  That's where she
discovered her first magic lamp.  A 54m² general store at DL5 yielded a
second (promptly transformed into Mjollnir), and a 30m² hardware store
on DL6 the third.  (And there are already two additional maces in the
game, no bones involved.  Pity they're so heavy and don't stack, I'd
just love to quiver them…)

